 instructions and cues.&#10;Set up&#10;1. Sit or stand tall with the weight at shoulder or chest height.&#10;2. Use a stable position and choose a load you can control.&#10;3. Brace your stomach and keep your feet planted.&#10;How to perform&#10;1. Press the weight up along a comfortable path.&#10;2. Stop when your arms are straight without shrugging.&#10;3. Lower slowly to the start and repeat.&#10;Coaching tips&#10;- Use a weight you can control.&#10;- Do not arch your back to finish a rep.&#10;- Lower the weight if your path changes.&#10;Reference media&#10;Use links for private references. Managed catalog media can refresh through content sync.&#10;Media links&#10;1 media item linked.&#10;Arnold Press thumbnail&#10;Link reference&#10;THUMBNAIL" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="true" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[0,1480][1080,2400]" drawing-order="0" hint="" /></node></node></node></node></node></node></node></node></node></node></hierarchy>